1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:03,920
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,927 --> 00:00:13,596
<i>Don't you know that I was</i>
<i>using her to find out?</i>

3
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:15,515
<i>-Find out what?</i>
<i>-I know she discovered something</i>

4
00:00:15,598 --> 00:00:17,475
<i>about your beloved Ivy!</i>

5
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:18,643
[Fernan] <i>Nimfa!</i>

6
00:00:18,727 --> 00:00:20,270
<i>-Nimfa!</i>
<i>-Mister Fernan!</i>

7
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,521
<i>-Nimfa!</i>
<i>-Mister Fernan!</i>

8
00:00:21,604 --> 00:00:24,399
[Camia] <i>Of all the places here</i>
<i>in Poblacion Ardiente,</i>

9
00:00:24,482 --> 00:00:27,485
<i>why did they put Nimfa's body</i>
<i>in front of your headquarters?</i>

10
00:00:27,569 --> 00:00:28,903
[Diego] <i>I can only think of two things.</i>

11
00:00:28,987 --> 00:00:31,156
<i>It's either they'll have me killed,</i>
<i>or have me framed.</i>

12
00:00:31,239 --> 00:00:33,408
-<i>I need to act fast.</i>
-[cops firing shots]

13
00:00:33,491 --> 00:00:35,660
[Julio] <i>Your inheritance, the armory,</i>

14
00:00:36,244 --> 00:00:37,704
<i>and everything in it.</i>

15
00:00:37,787 --> 00:00:41,750
<i>We almost lost everything</i>
<i>because of that bastard, Diego.</i>

16
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:42,667
[Arnaldo] <i>If you think…</i>

17
00:00:42,751 --> 00:00:45,170
<i>you can stop me from carrying out my plans</i>

18
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:47,922
<i>because of that raid, you're wrong.</i>

19
00:00:48,006 --> 00:00:51,009
<i>Mr. Torillo, we have a warrant</i>
<i>for your arrest</i>

20
00:00:51,092 --> 00:00:52,719
<i>for the murder of Nimfa Naig.</i>

21
00:00:52,802 --> 00:00:54,721
[Camia] <i>I'm sure the Ardientes</i>
<i>are behind this.</i>

22
00:00:54,804 --> 00:00:56,389
<i>They're afraid of losing the election.</i>

23
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:57,891
<i>That's why they're framing Diego.</i>

24
00:00:57,974 --> 00:00:58,850
[Diego] <i>I'm going with them.</i>

25
00:00:58,933 --> 00:01:01,352
<i>But we all know who really killed Nimfa.</i>

26
00:01:01,436 --> 00:01:04,898
<i>It was Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo,</i>
<i>and I will prove it!</i>

27
00:01:04,981 --> 00:01:07,734
[Fernan] <i>I just want someone to</i>
<i>pay for my daughter's death.</i>

28
00:01:07,817 --> 00:01:11,279
<i>And if it is Diego, prison</i>
<i>won't be enough as punishment.</i>

29
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:12,572
<i>What did you do to Diego?</i>

30
00:01:12,655 --> 00:01:15,033
[Arnaldo] <i>It was a frame-up.</i>
<i>And it was so easy.</i>

31
00:01:15,992 --> 00:01:19,245
<i>-That's enough!</i>
<i>-I'll kill him! You bastard!</i>

32
00:01:19,537 --> 00:01:22,373
[Camia] <i>Don't worry.</i>
<i>We'll look into your case,</i>

33
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:23,958
<i>so you won't have to stay here for long.</i>

34
00:01:24,042 --> 00:01:25,001
<i>-It's like you have…</i>
<i>-Ouch!</i>

35
00:01:25,084 --> 00:01:25,835
<i>so many secrets.</i>

36
00:01:25,919 --> 00:01:29,297
<i>Maybe Nimfa isn't the only one you killed.</i>

37
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:32,175
<i>I haven't killed anyone aside from Nimfa.</i>

38
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:36,137
<i>And I sent Diego to jail</i>
<i>so I'd stop feeling jealous.</i>

39
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:38,097
[Julio] <i>Tonight, I will end your misery.</i>

40
00:01:38,181 --> 00:01:39,474
<i>What do you mean?</i>

41
00:01:39,557 --> 00:01:42,602
<i>Just prepare a beautiful black dress.</i>

42
00:01:42,685 --> 00:01:43,978
[Raul] <i>Camia, he's my son.</i>

43
00:01:44,062 --> 00:01:46,397
<i>I have the right</i>
<i>to help him get out of here.</i>

44
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:49,150
<i>A father who blindly</i>
<i>follows the Ardientes.</i>

45
00:01:49,234 --> 00:01:51,611
<i>You won't prove anything to me or anyone</i>

46
00:01:51,694 --> 00:01:53,446
<i>as long as you're under</i>
<i>the Ardientes' thumb.</i>

47
00:01:53,530 --> 00:01:54,864
<i>-He wouldn't leave…</i>
<i>-Emilia.</i>

48
00:01:54,948 --> 00:01:57,325
<i>…our side. You know why, Camia?</i>

49
00:01:57,408 --> 00:01:59,035
<i>Because he's only mine.</i>

50
00:01:59,119 --> 00:02:00,036
[Arnaldo] <i>Grandpa, where are you?</i>

51
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:03,331
<i>I'm at Raul's final resting place.</i>

52
00:02:03,414 --> 00:02:05,125
<i>Well, you make sure you punish him good.</i>

53
00:02:05,208 --> 00:02:07,127
<i>Oh, don't worry. I will.</i>

54
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:11,422
Raul is all yours, Emilia.
No one's taking him from you.

55
00:02:11,506 --> 00:02:12,799
Really?

56
00:02:12,882 --> 00:02:14,843
You don't miss his handsome face?

57
00:02:15,593 --> 00:02:16,511
What about your--

58
00:02:16,594 --> 00:02:19,055
Say one more word
and I'll cut your tongue out!

59
00:02:19,139 --> 00:02:20,098
-Oh, really?
-Yes!

60
00:02:22,892 --> 00:02:24,894
[phone ringing]

61
00:02:25,520 --> 00:02:26,479
[Raul] Emilia, stop!

62
00:02:27,981 --> 00:02:29,399
-Emilia, that's enough!
-Give that back!

63
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:30,233
-Emilia, let's go!
-Oops!

64
00:02:30,316 --> 00:02:31,985
-Someone's calling.
-Emilia, give that back!

65
00:02:32,068 --> 00:02:33,695
-That's mine!
-Wait.

66
00:02:33,778 --> 00:02:35,071
Hey! A!

67
00:02:36,573 --> 00:02:38,241
A is calling. Is it…

68
00:02:38,324 --> 00:02:39,450
Lily Cruz?

69
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:41,077
Wait.

70
00:02:42,328 --> 00:02:43,705
Let me take it.

71
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:44,873
Hello?

72
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:47,000
Lily Cruz?

73
00:02:48,543 --> 00:02:49,544
<i>Lily Cruz?</i>

74
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:51,796
-Give that back!
-Hello, A?

75
00:02:53,381 --> 00:02:54,883
-Hello?
-I said…

76
00:02:54,966 --> 00:02:55,925
-There you go!
-Give that back!

77
00:02:58,428 --> 00:03:00,054
Shove it down your throat!

78
00:03:05,518 --> 00:03:08,688
Be thankful my husband
and my aunt were here to stop me,

79
00:03:08,771 --> 00:03:11,107
or I would've pulled all your hair out!

80
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:12,233
Let's go, Emilia.

81
00:03:15,862 --> 00:03:17,697
-[sighs heavily]
-Aunt Camia…

82
00:03:17,780 --> 00:03:18,781
are you okay?

83
00:03:19,240 --> 00:03:20,241
Yes, Diego.

84
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:25,580
Let's go, Mr. Torillo.

85
00:03:27,123 --> 00:03:28,291
-Auntie.
-Diego.

86
00:03:28,791 --> 00:03:30,043
-Attorney.
-Diego.

87
00:03:30,418 --> 00:03:31,377
Come here!

88
00:03:35,548 --> 00:03:36,549
Are you okay?

89
00:03:36,925 --> 00:03:38,384
Yes, attorney. Thank you.

90
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:43,223
-Come here!
-You're hurting me,

91
00:03:43,306 --> 00:03:44,432
-Raul!
-Why do you keep on…

92
00:03:44,515 --> 00:03:46,184
following me?

93
00:03:46,267 --> 00:03:48,311
This is my problem!
Mind your own business!

94
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:49,604
You're making things complicated!

95
00:03:49,938 --> 00:03:51,189
So, it's my fault?!

96
00:03:51,856 --> 00:03:54,150
You always think it's my fault!

97
00:03:54,234 --> 00:03:55,068
Isn't it?!

98
00:03:55,151 --> 00:03:57,612
You always think I'm the problem!

99
00:03:58,196 --> 00:03:59,656
You know what the real problem is?

100
00:04:00,073 --> 00:04:03,159
My love for you! That's the real problem.

101
00:04:03,701 --> 00:04:05,078
-Your love?
-I'm still holding on

102
00:04:05,161 --> 00:04:08,790
to the idea that you'll love me
back someday, Raul!

103
00:04:09,582 --> 00:04:11,376
But it seems like you never will.

104
00:04:12,502 --> 00:04:13,795
Papa's right.

105
00:04:14,879 --> 00:04:17,257
You make me miserable, Raul!

106
00:04:20,093 --> 00:04:22,720
That's not true. I did not make
your life miserable, Emilia.

107
00:04:22,804 --> 00:04:24,138
Your father did!

108
00:04:24,722 --> 00:04:26,849
You let him control our lives!

109
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:29,936
We could have lived
a simple life with the kids!

110
00:04:30,186 --> 00:04:32,563
It could have been just you,
me, Arnaldo, and Diego!

111
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:37,986
Even when they were kids,

112
00:04:38,069 --> 00:04:41,239
all they saw was greed and cruelty!

113
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,907
Your Papa taught them that!

114
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:44,200
That's why they turned out this way!

115
00:04:44,284 --> 00:04:46,703
Especially Arnaldo! He can't
even show you some compassion!

116
00:04:46,786 --> 00:04:48,538
My father and Arnaldo both love me!

117
00:04:48,621 --> 00:04:51,791
Do you seriously believe
your father loves you?!

118
00:04:51,874 --> 00:04:53,167
Really?

119
00:04:53,251 --> 00:04:55,712
I'm the only one
who still loves you, Emilia!

120
00:04:55,795 --> 00:04:58,006
-[Emilia crying]
-[Raul] Okay?

121
00:04:58,089 --> 00:05:00,133
And if your father really loved you,

122
00:05:00,216 --> 00:05:02,302
why didn't he ask you to run for governor?

123
00:05:02,385 --> 00:05:04,762
Why'd he ask Arnaldo?
Aren't you supposed to be better?!

124
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:06,139
You're more experienced!

125
00:05:08,016 --> 00:05:09,100
Love, my ass!

126
00:05:09,183 --> 00:05:10,393
[Claire] Raul, that's enough.

127
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:12,437
[Emilia wailing]

128
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:17,775
I'm always…

129
00:05:20,695 --> 00:05:22,697
[Emilia weeping]

130
00:05:33,791 --> 00:05:36,127
-Wait, what's this about?!
-Mr. Raul, you need to come with us.

131
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:38,421
-Wait! What's going on?!
-The congressman sent us.

132
00:05:38,504 --> 00:05:40,506
Wait. He's not going.

133
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:42,133
Raul, please, you have to go.

134
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:44,844
-No.
-No. Arnaldo deserved it.

135
00:05:44,927 --> 00:05:46,345
Our son needed to be taught a lesson!

136
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:48,014
I'm coming too!

137
00:05:48,097 --> 00:05:50,099
[tense music playing]

138
00:05:58,691 --> 00:05:59,692
Papa,

139
00:05:59,776 --> 00:06:00,860
you wanted to see me?

140
00:06:01,402 --> 00:06:02,612
[Julio scoffs]

141
00:06:02,695 --> 00:06:05,114
Such cockiness, Raul.

142
00:06:05,865 --> 00:06:06,991
I like that.

143
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:11,788
And I do hope you stay that way
when I make you pay

144
00:06:11,871 --> 00:06:15,291
for what you did to Arnaldo.

145
00:06:16,084 --> 00:06:17,168
Well,

146
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:19,170
what you see is what you get.

147
00:06:19,253 --> 00:06:20,546
Choose one here.

148
00:06:21,255 --> 00:06:22,715
Which one should I use?

149
00:06:23,466 --> 00:06:24,926
Maybe the good old. 45?

150
00:06:26,844 --> 00:06:28,721
One bullet between your eyes…

151
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:30,681
Done.

152
00:06:31,057 --> 00:06:32,058
Or…

153
00:06:33,726 --> 00:06:34,811
Maybe the long arm.

154
00:06:35,394 --> 00:06:36,771
I could make you suffer a little.

155
00:06:38,397 --> 00:06:39,774
But, if you want…

156
00:06:42,360 --> 00:06:43,694
I could use this knife!

157
00:06:43,778 --> 00:06:45,696
I'll stab you until you bleed out.

158
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:46,906
[Emilia] No, please, Papa.

159
00:06:46,989 --> 00:06:48,074
Don't punish Raul.

160
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:52,328
He only did that to discipline Arnaldo.

161
00:06:53,162 --> 00:06:54,247
[Raul] Papa,

162
00:06:54,330 --> 00:06:55,498
Arnaldo is my son.

163
00:06:56,249 --> 00:06:58,960
And as his father, I have
the right to discipline my own.

164
00:06:59,043 --> 00:07:00,920
He was disrespecting me and Emilia!

165
00:07:01,379 --> 00:07:03,673
He doesn't even respect us as his parents!

166
00:07:05,716 --> 00:07:06,801
Only I…

167
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:12,765
have the right to discipline Arnaldo.

168
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:13,808
No, Papa!

169
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:17,186
We are his parents!
It is our responsibility

170
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:18,729
to instill some discipline in Arnaldo!

171
00:07:19,313 --> 00:07:20,398
Please!

172
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:25,194
Don't give me that
crappy concerned parent card!

173
00:07:26,028 --> 00:07:29,449
It's not like you were
ever good parents to him!

174
00:07:29,782 --> 00:07:31,492
That's because you didn't give us a chance

175
00:07:31,576 --> 00:07:32,952
to become parents to him!

176
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:37,915
You took him as your own
because you never had a son!

177
00:07:37,999 --> 00:07:40,668
So, what if I did? Hmm?

178
00:07:41,169 --> 00:07:42,086
Look at him now!

179
00:07:42,753 --> 00:07:45,423
See how successful he has become.

180
00:07:46,090 --> 00:07:47,049
[Julio scoffs]

181
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:48,801
If I had trusted you two to raise him,

182
00:07:49,635 --> 00:07:51,679
he'd be a vendor on the streets!

183
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:56,100
So, he's successful…
But, how'd he turn out?!

184
00:07:56,601 --> 00:07:59,020
He's no different than you!
He's a criminal now!

185
00:07:59,103 --> 00:08:02,899
-Kill this insolent bastard!
-Papa! Papa, don't! Don't!

186
00:08:02,982 --> 00:08:04,734
-No, Papa, please!
-How brave.

187
00:08:05,401 --> 00:08:06,569
Papa,

188
00:08:06,652 --> 00:08:10,198
if you're going to kill Raul, kill me too.

189
00:08:10,281 --> 00:08:11,491
-Please.
-What?

190
00:08:13,075 --> 00:08:13,951
Please, Papa.

191
00:08:14,035 --> 00:08:16,996
-Get out of the way!
-No, don't.

192
00:08:17,079 --> 00:08:18,206
Emilia, just leave. Come on, let go.

193
00:08:18,289 --> 00:08:20,249
Get out of here, Raul.

194
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:21,751
-Leave.
-I'm not going anywhere.

195
00:08:21,834 --> 00:08:23,085
Leave!

196
00:08:25,254 --> 00:08:27,048
Please leave.

197
00:08:28,216 --> 00:08:32,178
You're crazy, Emilia! You are plain loco!

198
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:35,806
Someday, you will regret all of these.

199
00:08:36,974 --> 00:08:38,017
I don't think so!

200
00:08:38,100 --> 00:08:40,186
-Oh, yes!
-I'll enjoy it.

201
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:42,230
But I'll never regret it.

202
00:08:43,898 --> 00:08:45,066
Bunch of fools!

203
00:08:47,818 --> 00:08:48,819
[exhales sharply]

204
00:08:53,658 --> 00:08:55,535
-Sir, Miss Ivy isn't here.
-What?!

205
00:08:55,993 --> 00:08:57,912
-She's not--
-Louder! I can't hear you!

206
00:08:57,995 --> 00:08:59,997
-Sir, she isn't home.
-She's out?

207
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:01,624
-Yes, sir.
-Then get out of my sight.

208
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:11,175
<i>Where'd you go again, Ivy?</i>

209
00:09:13,469 --> 00:09:14,679
<i>To Diego?</i>

210
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:24,480
Lily, I'm worried about Diego.

211
00:09:24,897 --> 00:09:26,566
He needs to get out of that prison

212
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:29,652
because I know the Ardientes
are plotting to get rid of him.

213
00:09:30,486 --> 00:09:32,280
Diego's getting out soon, Mom.

214
00:09:32,613 --> 00:09:34,282
Because I have the evidence…

215
00:09:34,865 --> 00:09:36,075
that will set him free.

216
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:38,160
[Arnaldo] <i>No.</i>

217
00:09:38,244 --> 00:09:41,289
<i>I haven't killed anyone aside from Nimfa.</i>

218
00:09:44,208 --> 00:09:46,294
Wait, if you release this, that means…

219
00:09:46,377 --> 00:09:47,670
I'll reveal my true identity.

220
00:09:50,131 --> 00:09:52,300
I will tell the world that I am Lily.

221
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:54,844
-No…
-Mom.

222
00:09:54,927 --> 00:09:58,180
That's the only way
I can think of to help Diego

223
00:09:58,264 --> 00:10:00,433
and put a stop to Arnaldo's ruthlessness.

224
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:05,021
Lily's coming back,

225
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:06,772
so they better watch out.

226
00:10:21,203 --> 00:10:22,204
Emilia?

227
00:10:27,043 --> 00:10:28,127
You know, Auntie,

228
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:29,128
Raul is right.

229
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:32,381
Papa destroyed us all.

230
00:10:33,841 --> 00:10:34,675
And I'm sure…

231
00:10:35,426 --> 00:10:36,552
his enemies…

232
00:10:37,011 --> 00:10:38,596
will stand against him.

233
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:42,350
[tense music playing]

234
00:10:51,651 --> 00:10:52,652
[Natalie] Raul?

235
00:10:54,028 --> 00:10:56,530
You seem so restless
ever since you came back here.

236
00:10:57,990 --> 00:10:59,200
Is there a problem?

237
00:11:05,539 --> 00:11:08,167
It's time to bring the Ardientes down.

238
00:11:10,127 --> 00:11:11,253
Finally!

239
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:15,216
I've longed to face your wife!

240
00:11:15,925 --> 00:11:17,510
What do you think I should do to her?

241
00:11:18,761 --> 00:11:19,929
Shave her head?

242
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:22,098
Have her raped?

243
00:11:22,681 --> 00:11:24,100
Or better yet,

244
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:26,936
should I shoot her as many times

245
00:11:27,019 --> 00:11:28,396
as she shot my father?

246
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:33,567
I'm so excited!

247
00:11:43,077 --> 00:11:44,078
Rufo.

248
00:11:45,496 --> 00:11:46,622
Go to your boss.

249
00:11:47,915 --> 00:11:49,375
Tell him I want to meet up.

250
00:11:50,793 --> 00:11:51,961
We need to talk.

251
00:11:53,421 --> 00:11:55,131
I'll need a lot of men.

252
00:12:04,306 --> 00:12:05,641
<i>Hold on, Diego.</i>

253
00:12:05,724 --> 00:12:07,351
<i>I'll get you out of prison…</i>

254
00:12:08,477 --> 00:12:09,437
<i>my son.</i>

255
00:12:12,064 --> 00:12:14,191
How did that bastard leave
without a scratch?

256
00:12:14,817 --> 00:12:16,444
His time will come.

257
00:12:17,153 --> 00:12:18,154
But when?

258
00:12:18,612 --> 00:12:20,030
When he finally gets away?

259
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:23,033
Or when he gets Diego out of prison?

260
00:12:23,117 --> 00:12:24,160
[Julio chuckling]

261
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:29,498
He does not have the power
nor the capacity to do that.

262
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:32,626
Okay, but what if Mom helps him?

263
00:12:32,710 --> 00:12:34,712
Oh, Emilia.

264
00:12:35,629 --> 00:12:39,216
Emilia, your mother, can be
stupid at times because of love.

265
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:42,595
But she's not stupid enough to do anything

266
00:12:42,678 --> 00:12:45,055
that would ruin our family.

267
00:12:45,139 --> 00:12:48,058
[Arnaldo laughing]

268
00:12:48,142 --> 00:12:49,477
You don't know that.

269
00:12:50,352 --> 00:12:53,355
People can really do
stupid things because of love.

270
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:59,320
Are we still talking about Emilia or…

271
00:13:01,530 --> 00:13:02,573
your fiancée?

272
00:13:07,161 --> 00:13:08,287
I don't know, Grandpa.

273
00:13:09,663 --> 00:13:11,790
I feel Ivy is keeping
her true relationship

274
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:13,417
with Diego a secret.

275
00:13:13,501 --> 00:13:14,585
Hmm…

276
00:13:15,419 --> 00:13:16,420
Well,

277
00:13:17,379 --> 00:13:19,173
there's only one way to find out.

278
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:22,384
Test her.

279
00:13:23,385 --> 00:13:24,220
How?

280
00:13:25,971 --> 00:13:26,889
Use Diego.

281
00:13:26,972 --> 00:13:30,851
[tense music playing]

282
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:39,235
[cop] All right punks!

283
00:13:39,318 --> 00:13:40,402
Go to sleep!

284
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:43,864
[tense music playing]

285
00:14:05,886 --> 00:14:08,180
-[grunts]
-[thuds]

286
00:14:12,476 --> 00:14:14,395
[grunting]

287
00:14:16,981 --> 00:14:17,982
[groans]

288
00:14:24,113 --> 00:14:25,114
Diego.

289
00:14:25,781 --> 00:14:27,032
Diego.

290
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:28,117
Diego!

291
00:14:29,618 --> 00:14:30,703
-Lily…
-Diego!

292
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:32,955
Mom, they're beating Diego up.

293
00:14:33,038 --> 00:14:34,957
Something bad is happening to Diego.

294
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:36,667
Lily, you're just dreaming.

295
00:14:39,253 --> 00:14:40,421
Who are you?

296
00:14:40,504 --> 00:14:41,547
What do you want from me?

297
00:14:41,630 --> 00:14:42,798
Get him!

298
00:14:45,092 --> 00:14:47,636
-[thuds]
-[grunts]

299
00:14:49,096 --> 00:14:50,097
[grunts]

300
00:14:53,475 --> 00:14:55,561
-[thuds]
-[grunts]

301
00:15:02,651 --> 00:15:05,029
[Ivy] Mom, I don't know what I
would do if something…

302
00:15:05,112 --> 00:15:07,031
happens to Diego.

303
00:15:09,491 --> 00:15:11,493
-[grunts]
-[thuds]

304
00:15:14,455 --> 00:15:15,539
[Camia] <i>Lily.</i>

305
00:15:15,873 --> 00:15:17,291
<i>Diego is safe.</i>

306
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:20,502
He's strong.
Nothing bad will happen to him.

307
00:15:27,509 --> 00:15:29,929
-[thuds]
-[grunts]

308
00:15:31,555 --> 00:15:33,474
[grunting]

309
00:15:42,608 --> 00:15:44,777
[action music playing]

310
00:15:55,746 --> 00:15:57,957
-[screaming]
-[grunts]

311
00:16:06,256 --> 00:16:07,591
[detainee groaning]

312
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:10,803
Who hired you?

313
00:16:11,929 --> 00:16:13,305
Who hired you?!

314
00:16:15,349 --> 00:16:16,433
The police.

315
00:16:26,193 --> 00:16:28,070
Here's what you requested
last night, Mayor.

316
00:16:28,445 --> 00:16:29,738
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

317
00:16:34,535 --> 00:16:38,080
I'm so excited to see Diego's
bruises when I visit him.

318
00:16:38,497 --> 00:16:39,498
[scoffs]

319
00:16:40,124 --> 00:16:41,583
Do you think Miss Aguas…

320
00:16:42,668 --> 00:16:43,669
is excited too?

321
00:16:45,671 --> 00:16:46,672
We'll see.

322
00:16:47,923 --> 00:16:48,882
We'll see.

323
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:50,592
[Ivy] Please schedule a conference call…

324
00:16:50,676 --> 00:16:51,760
with the engineering team.

325
00:16:51,844 --> 00:16:55,055
Tell them we have something
to discuss, okay?

326
00:16:55,139 --> 00:16:57,224
-Yes, Miss Aguas. Excuse me.
-Thank you. You may go.

327
00:16:59,643 --> 00:17:00,644
Hello, Attorney.

328
00:17:01,103 --> 00:17:03,063
[Georgina] I just heard
Arnaldo's confession.

329
00:17:03,564 --> 00:17:06,108
But it'll only hold in court
if you testify against him.

330
00:17:06,191 --> 00:17:08,193
Then, I'll do just that. No problem.

331
00:17:08,610 --> 00:17:10,821
Like your mother said, it's too risky.

332
00:17:10,904 --> 00:17:12,740
Besides, there are lots of other methods…

333
00:17:12,823 --> 00:17:14,158
-to delay the case.
-So, tell me…

334
00:17:14,241 --> 00:17:16,326
what other methods are, Attorney.

335
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:18,954
First, we need to look
for a new venue for the hearing.

336
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:21,457
And then, I'll pressure the current judge

337
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:24,084
to inhibit the case,
so we can look for a new judge

338
00:17:24,168 --> 00:17:25,169
to preside over it.

339
00:17:25,627 --> 00:17:27,713
Okay, you go do that.

340
00:17:27,796 --> 00:17:28,797
Meanwhile,

341
00:17:28,881 --> 00:17:31,216
I'll look for more
solid evidence that'll prove

342
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:33,677
Arnaldo killed Nimfa.

343
00:17:33,761 --> 00:17:35,012
[phone ringing]

344
00:17:35,971 --> 00:17:37,264
Speak of the devil.

345
00:17:37,347 --> 00:17:38,515
[phone ringing]

346
00:17:38,891 --> 00:17:39,892
Have a seat, Attorney.

347
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:41,894
Hon?

348
00:17:42,603 --> 00:17:43,729
Hey, hon.

349
00:17:43,812 --> 00:17:44,688
Where are you?

350
00:17:45,606 --> 00:17:47,941
I'm sorry, hon.
I know you went to my place last night.

351
00:17:48,025 --> 00:17:51,445
But I forgot to tell you I went to Manila.

352
00:17:51,528 --> 00:17:54,156
<i>I had to take care of something for work.</i>

353
00:17:54,990 --> 00:17:57,493
Anyway, don't worry.
I'm on my way back to you.

354
00:17:57,576 --> 00:17:58,619
<i>Did you miss me?</i>

355
00:17:58,702 --> 00:18:01,121
Well, yes. I missed you.

356
00:18:02,206 --> 00:18:04,500
That's why we need to meet up later.

357
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:05,375
It's important.

358
00:18:06,043 --> 00:18:07,211
<i>Meet me at the office?</i>

359
00:18:07,711 --> 00:18:09,463
Okay, hon. See you.

360
00:18:12,674 --> 00:18:13,675
[mockingly] Hello, hon?

361
00:18:14,176 --> 00:18:15,260
I missed you!

362
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:17,179
How sweet.

363
00:18:18,388 --> 00:18:19,389
Lovebirds.

364
00:18:22,810 --> 00:18:27,773
Mom, Attorney, I have to go and
meet my fake, criminal fiancé.

365
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:32,861
Dear, take care of yourself, okay?

366
00:18:34,321 --> 00:18:37,241
Mom, please tell Diego
we're doing everything we can

367
00:18:37,324 --> 00:18:38,951
to get him out of prison.

368
00:18:40,869 --> 00:18:41,954
See you, Attorney.

369
00:18:49,545 --> 00:18:50,546
Mayor.

370
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:53,132
Good afternoon.

371
00:18:56,093 --> 00:18:57,094
Hey.

372
00:18:57,719 --> 00:18:58,720
Are you surprised?

373
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:00,472
Sorry, I forgot to mention

374
00:19:00,556 --> 00:19:02,724
we were visiting
my beloved brother, Diego.

375
00:19:04,810 --> 00:19:06,353
I'm honestly more worried…

376
00:19:07,604 --> 00:19:09,773
about seeing my former friend

377
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:12,526
turned criminal.

378
00:19:13,652 --> 00:19:14,820
I mean, what if…

379
00:19:15,779 --> 00:19:17,322
What if he suddenly attacks us?

380
00:19:17,656 --> 00:19:18,657
I'm scared.

381
00:19:21,118 --> 00:19:22,286
Don't worry.

382
00:19:22,369 --> 00:19:23,495
Just stay close to me.

383
00:19:24,580 --> 00:19:25,789
Okay?

384
00:19:25,873 --> 00:19:28,125
No one will hurt you
as long as I'm around.

385
00:19:30,794 --> 00:19:31,795
Let's go?

386
00:19:44,683 --> 00:19:46,768
[tense music playing]

387
00:19:51,356 --> 00:19:53,775
-All right, leave us.
-Yes, Mayor.

388
00:20:00,657 --> 00:20:03,118
Looks like you woke up
on the wrong side of the bed.

389
00:20:06,538 --> 00:20:07,998
You're covered in bruises.

390
00:20:08,081 --> 00:20:09,249
Did you fall off your bed?

391
00:20:09,708 --> 00:20:11,585
Those men you hired to beat me up…

392
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:14,671
Aren't you going to ask about them?

393
00:20:15,797 --> 00:20:17,382
They're in the hospital, by the way.

394
00:20:18,258 --> 00:20:20,469
You might want to pay them a visit later.

395
00:20:20,552 --> 00:20:21,637
Wow!

396
00:20:23,388 --> 00:20:24,473
Nice one.

397
00:20:24,973 --> 00:20:27,184
You've got guts for a prisoner.

398
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:29,561
Well, I'd rather have guts…

399
00:20:30,646 --> 00:20:32,981
than be a spineless coward.

400
00:20:33,065 --> 00:20:34,441
Are you calling me a coward?

401
00:20:35,234 --> 00:20:36,652
Well? Is that it?

402
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:39,446
I'm no coward, Diego.

403
00:20:40,489 --> 00:20:41,615
I'm no coward.

404
00:20:43,825 --> 00:20:45,077
Then prove it.

405
00:20:47,287 --> 00:20:48,330
Prove it!

406
00:20:50,791 --> 00:20:52,000
[scoffs]

407
00:20:52,084 --> 00:20:53,543
Fight me fair and square.

408
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:56,713
Fight?

409
00:20:58,215 --> 00:20:59,299
You want me to fight you?

410
00:21:00,550 --> 00:21:01,677
I don't have to.

411
00:21:01,760 --> 00:21:04,096
I've already won, and you've already lost.

412
00:21:05,097 --> 00:21:07,182
Who would vote for a criminal
like you, huh?

413
00:21:08,225 --> 00:21:09,142
No one.

414
00:21:09,226 --> 00:21:12,187
And I'm going to make sure
you rot here in jail.

415
00:21:14,106 --> 00:21:15,274
You're never getting out.

416
00:21:16,108 --> 00:21:17,025
Remember that.

417
00:21:19,027 --> 00:21:20,195
Oh, by the way.

418
00:21:21,321 --> 00:21:23,115
I also came…

419
00:21:24,074 --> 00:21:25,075
to give you this.

420
00:21:26,201 --> 00:21:27,202
Here.

421
00:21:29,788 --> 00:21:31,540
I'll just leave this here, okay?

422
00:21:33,792 --> 00:21:35,502
Ivy and I are inviting you…

423
00:21:36,795 --> 00:21:38,088
to our engagement party.

424
00:21:39,715 --> 00:21:41,675
But I know you won't make it.

425
00:21:43,343 --> 00:21:44,553
You know why?

426
00:21:53,562 --> 00:21:54,938
Because I'm finishing you off right here.

427
00:21:59,067 --> 00:22:00,944
You. Will. Die. Here--

428
00:22:07,117 --> 00:22:10,454
[Arnaldo grunting]

429
00:22:14,708 --> 00:22:19,004
Oh! Diego! Diego! Stop it! Diego!

430
00:22:19,671 --> 00:22:21,089
Diego, stop!

431
00:22:21,715 --> 00:22:23,008
Diego, let go!

432
00:22:23,842 --> 00:22:24,634
Diego!

433
00:22:24,718 --> 00:22:26,928
-Hon!
-[Arnaldo panting]

434
00:22:30,849 --> 00:22:32,559
-Hon!
-[Arnaldo panting]

435
00:22:33,935 --> 00:22:35,395
Hon, are you okay?

436
00:22:39,191 --> 00:22:40,817
Bring that bastard back to his cell.

437
00:22:42,235 --> 00:22:43,820
-[Arnaldo coughs]
-Hon.

438
00:22:46,782 --> 00:22:47,783
This isn't over.

439
00:22:53,121 --> 00:22:53,955
[Georgina] That's right.

440
00:22:54,581 --> 00:22:56,583
All of the allegations against my client,

441
00:22:56,666 --> 00:22:59,419
Mr. Diego Torillo, are false.

442
00:22:59,878 --> 00:23:01,797
Diego is an honest and decent man.

443
00:23:01,880 --> 00:23:05,717
And that's how the people
of Ardiente know him too.

444
00:23:06,468 --> 00:23:08,470
[Arnaldo clapping]

445
00:23:11,431 --> 00:23:12,599
Nice.

446
00:23:12,682 --> 00:23:15,477
If what you're saying is true,
then make sure you win the case.

447
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:17,854
We'll win the case because the allegations

448
00:23:17,938 --> 00:23:19,564
against my client are based on lies.

449
00:23:19,648 --> 00:23:20,774
Whoa.

450
00:23:21,274 --> 00:23:22,275
Careful.

451
00:23:22,609 --> 00:23:23,944
That statement's libelous.

452
00:23:24,361 --> 00:23:25,654
I can file a complaint.

453
00:23:25,737 --> 00:23:27,239
I am not afraid of the law.

454
00:23:28,240 --> 00:23:30,575
I memorized the entire
Philippine Constitution.

455
00:23:30,909 --> 00:23:32,077
And I'm telling you now,

456
00:23:32,452 --> 00:23:35,497
I can prove that everything
I just said isn't libelous,

457
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:37,290
but factual and true.

458
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:39,126
And when I'm done doing that,

459
00:23:39,459 --> 00:23:40,752
I'll go after you…

460
00:23:41,294 --> 00:23:43,004
for the murder of Nimfa Naig.

461
00:23:43,088 --> 00:23:45,090
[tense music playing]

462
00:24:09,364 --> 00:24:10,365
Ivy.

463
00:24:12,659 --> 00:24:14,661
[tense music playing]

464
00:24:38,059 --> 00:24:39,769
You're too strong
for your own good, Attorney.

465
00:24:40,270 --> 00:24:41,271
Be careful.

466
00:24:41,605 --> 00:24:43,607
Someone might put you in your place.

467
00:24:44,733 --> 00:24:46,151
I am immune to threats.

468
00:24:46,776 --> 00:24:48,612
I eat them for breakfast,
lunch, and dinner.

469
00:24:49,154 --> 00:24:51,281
And I only strive to win harder when…

470
00:24:51,364 --> 00:24:52,782
someone threatens me.

471
00:24:52,866 --> 00:24:54,201
[chuckles] Win?

472
00:24:55,493 --> 00:24:57,329
I think it's too early for that.

473
00:24:57,412 --> 00:24:59,122
Let's wait for the case to start first.

474
00:24:59,206 --> 00:25:00,373
And it will.

475
00:25:00,457 --> 00:25:02,751
But not in this puppet court
you have under your control.

476
00:25:02,834 --> 00:25:04,461
Let's do it fair and square.

477
00:25:04,544 --> 00:25:07,047
The way I see it, no matter
where we bring this case,

478
00:25:07,130 --> 00:25:09,174
there will only be one outcome.

479
00:25:09,257 --> 00:25:13,345
Diego killed Nimfa,
according to the evidence.

480
00:25:14,054 --> 00:25:15,388
Mayor Torillo…

481
00:25:15,931 --> 00:25:16,806
That's enough.

482
00:25:17,432 --> 00:25:19,726
Let's put a stop to this.
This argument won't go anywhere.

483
00:25:19,809 --> 00:25:21,895
That's why I'd like to propose something.

484
00:25:21,978 --> 00:25:24,356
Let's do a pre-election survey.

485
00:25:24,439 --> 00:25:27,025
Whoever wins there is the one
who's telling the truth.

486
00:25:27,108 --> 00:25:28,985
Now, who are they going to choose?

487
00:25:29,069 --> 00:25:30,278
A criminal…

488
00:25:30,779 --> 00:25:32,739
or an honest politician like me?

489
00:25:34,157 --> 00:25:35,450
Let them decide.

490
00:25:37,661 --> 00:25:38,536
Hey.

491
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:40,538
Why did you go quiet all of a sudden?

492
00:25:40,622 --> 00:25:43,166
Because we know
you'll manipulate the survey

493
00:25:43,250 --> 00:25:44,709
to incriminate Diego further.

494
00:25:46,795 --> 00:25:48,171
Let's go, Attorney.

495
00:26:05,480 --> 00:26:06,314
Hon?

496
00:26:08,942 --> 00:26:09,943
Hon.

497
00:26:10,902 --> 00:26:12,362
Sorry, I had to use the restroom.

498
00:26:12,445 --> 00:26:13,613
Okay.

499
00:26:13,697 --> 00:26:17,325
Mayor, do you think you will win
the survey and the election?

500
00:26:17,409 --> 00:26:18,576
Definitely.

501
00:26:19,160 --> 00:26:20,704
Right, my future wife?

502
00:26:20,787 --> 00:26:22,205
My future first lady.

503
00:26:22,747 --> 00:26:23,665
Of course.

504
00:26:24,207 --> 00:26:26,084
[Ivy] <i>No one else will win</i>

505
00:26:26,167 --> 00:26:29,254
<i>other than Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

506
00:26:29,337 --> 00:26:30,797
He's the only one who should.

507
00:26:31,840 --> 00:26:32,882
See?

508
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:34,217
<i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

509
00:26:35,135 --> 00:26:36,261
<i>Excuse me.</i>

510
00:26:36,344 --> 00:26:39,180
[upbeat music playing]

511
00:26:42,225 --> 00:26:44,477
[clapping]

512
00:26:44,561 --> 00:26:46,688
[Julio] This is perfect.

513
00:26:47,897 --> 00:26:51,067
I'm sure Arnaldo's ratings will go up.

514
00:26:51,901 --> 00:26:53,445
You are so right, Papa.

515
00:26:53,945 --> 00:26:56,698
You know, Ivy makes Arnaldo desirable.

516
00:26:56,781 --> 00:26:58,033
[chuckles]

517
00:26:58,783 --> 00:27:00,994
Something you could never achieve

518
00:27:01,077 --> 00:27:03,455
with your dog-faced husband, Raul.

519
00:27:05,123 --> 00:27:09,169
Papa, can we please move on?
He already moved out, right?

520
00:27:09,252 --> 00:27:14,132
What we need to focus on now
is the search for Lily Cruz.

521
00:27:15,925 --> 00:27:16,926
Why?

522
00:27:18,261 --> 00:27:19,929
Do you know where to find her?

523
00:27:21,848 --> 00:27:22,766
Not yet, Papa.

524
00:27:23,475 --> 00:27:25,852
But I'll make sure when I come back,

525
00:27:25,935 --> 00:27:27,771
I'll have their heads with me,

526
00:27:27,854 --> 00:27:30,190
so my headache can finally go away.

527
00:27:30,273 --> 00:27:31,900
So, if you'll excuse me…

528
00:27:35,362 --> 00:27:38,073
Those two women are going headhunting?

529
00:27:38,573 --> 00:27:39,574
[scoffs]

530
00:27:43,078 --> 00:27:44,788
I need more men.

531
00:27:45,330 --> 00:27:46,748
And they have to be good.

532
00:27:47,248 --> 00:27:48,958
I'm planning something big.

533
00:27:49,042 --> 00:27:50,919
Is that all? I'll send my men…

534
00:27:51,002 --> 00:27:52,504
<i>first thing in the morning.</i>

535
00:27:52,587 --> 00:27:55,799
That's what I like about you.
You're sharp and dependable.

536
00:27:55,882 --> 00:27:56,966
That's the agreement.

537
00:27:57,050 --> 00:27:59,177
You supply the money,
and I supply the men.

538
00:27:59,677 --> 00:28:00,804
<i>We'll both benefit.</i>

539
00:28:00,887 --> 00:28:02,055
And we'll both flourish.

540
00:28:02,722 --> 00:28:03,848
You can count on me.

541
00:28:04,432 --> 00:28:05,558
<i>So don't think twice about…</i>

542
00:28:05,642 --> 00:28:06,726
betraying me, Jaguar.

543
00:28:07,227 --> 00:28:09,854
We're partners when it comes
to taking down the Ardientes.

544
00:28:10,188 --> 00:28:12,315
That's why you can't have all the fun.

545
00:28:13,316 --> 00:28:15,318
[tense music playing]

546
00:28:22,325 --> 00:28:23,952
Gather all our men.

547
00:28:25,078 --> 00:28:27,914
And round up every judge in Ardiente.

548
00:28:29,207 --> 00:28:31,126
Tell them I need to talk to them.

549
00:28:31,543 --> 00:28:32,877
Okay, Jaguar. I'm on it.

550
00:28:39,926 --> 00:28:40,927
Thank you.

551
00:28:46,182 --> 00:28:49,310
[somber music playing]

552
00:28:55,775 --> 00:28:57,777
So, where is Raul, Emilia?

553
00:28:58,778 --> 00:28:59,821
I don't know, Auntie.

554
00:29:00,780 --> 00:29:02,031
He'll be gone for a while.

555
00:29:02,657 --> 00:29:03,742
And while he's away,

556
00:29:04,784 --> 00:29:08,663
I will eliminate everyone
who stands against our love.

557
00:29:09,956 --> 00:29:11,708
First, Camia Cruz.

558
00:29:12,542 --> 00:29:14,919
Then, that pest, Lily Cruz.

559
00:29:15,003 --> 00:29:18,047
Because I know she's going to
come after me and Raul one day.

560
00:29:18,715 --> 00:29:20,258
And then, Papa.

561
00:29:20,341 --> 00:29:24,512
If he continues to disapprove of our love.

562
00:29:27,515 --> 00:29:30,560
You're willing to do all that for Raul.

563
00:29:31,728 --> 00:29:32,729
But, how about him?

564
00:29:33,563 --> 00:29:35,482
What can he do for you?

565
00:29:36,858 --> 00:29:37,942
Auntie,

566
00:29:38,401 --> 00:29:40,069
some relationships are one-sided.

567
00:29:40,445 --> 00:29:42,238
Just like Mama and Papa's.

568
00:29:42,322 --> 00:29:43,782
Don't you agree?

569
00:29:45,074 --> 00:29:46,117
And…

570
00:29:46,201 --> 00:29:47,744
I'm making the same mistake.

571
00:29:49,913 --> 00:29:51,456
But why, hmm?

572
00:29:52,791 --> 00:29:55,168
Because it's the only kind of love I know,

573
00:29:55,877 --> 00:29:59,798
and it's the kind of love
that makes me happy, Auntie.

574
00:30:01,216 --> 00:30:04,302
[tense music playing]

575
00:30:13,603 --> 00:30:14,646
He's here.

576
00:30:17,565 --> 00:30:19,025
-[man] Yes, ma'am?
-[Emilia] Sit down.

577
00:30:23,112 --> 00:30:26,074
I wasn't asking you
to look for Harry Potter.

578
00:30:26,157 --> 00:30:27,867
Finding a lead shouldn't be this hard!

579
00:30:30,286 --> 00:30:31,412
I'm sorry, ma'am.

580
00:30:31,871 --> 00:30:33,873
I swear, I'll find her.

581
00:30:33,957 --> 00:30:36,501
You're sorry? Well, I'm bored.

582
00:30:36,960 --> 00:30:38,211
Update me, okay?

583
00:30:38,294 --> 00:30:39,963
-Yes, ma'am.
-Or else…

584
00:30:40,505 --> 00:30:41,798
I'll have someone finish you off.

585
00:30:41,881 --> 00:30:43,591
You know what I'm capable of.

586
00:30:43,675 --> 00:30:44,634
Yes, ma'am.

587
00:30:44,717 --> 00:30:45,927
Now, go!

588
00:30:49,931 --> 00:30:52,267
I can't believe I'm paying him that much.

589
00:30:58,231 --> 00:31:01,150
What are you up to, Emilia?

590
00:31:03,736 --> 00:31:05,405
Who are you looking for?

591
00:31:10,118 --> 00:31:11,202
[line ringing]

592
00:31:11,286 --> 00:31:12,287
Hello?

593
00:31:14,831 --> 00:31:16,624
I have a project for you.

594
00:31:23,423 --> 00:31:25,425
[tense music playing]

595
00:31:28,887 --> 00:31:31,931
They're scared I'll win the elections.

596
00:31:32,015 --> 00:31:33,641
That's why they set this whole thing up.

597
00:31:33,725 --> 00:31:36,352
They framed me
for the murder of Nimfa Naig.

598
00:31:36,436 --> 00:31:38,438
Why would they do that to you?

599
00:31:38,521 --> 00:31:40,690
To ensure that their side will win.

600
00:31:40,773 --> 00:31:42,734
Don't you know how the Ardientes operate?

601
00:31:42,817 --> 00:31:47,530
They'll do everything
to hold on to their power.

602
00:31:47,614 --> 00:31:50,366
Does that mean you're accepting
Mayor Arnaldo's challenge

603
00:31:50,450 --> 00:31:52,243
to participate in a pre-election survey?

604
00:31:52,327 --> 00:31:53,328
Yes.

605
00:31:54,037 --> 00:31:55,413
Because I believe…

606
00:31:56,080 --> 00:31:57,415
that even if I'm behind bars,

607
00:31:57,916 --> 00:32:00,919
my supporters will remain loyal to me.

608
00:32:06,716 --> 00:32:08,676
I am not going to reshape Ardiente.

609
00:32:09,260 --> 00:32:10,261
You are.

610
00:32:11,346 --> 00:32:13,014
If you really love our province,

611
00:32:13,681 --> 00:32:15,016
you'll choose what is right.

612
00:32:16,142 --> 00:32:18,102
You will choose change.

613
00:32:21,147 --> 00:32:23,816
For a town where the people
hold more power

614
00:32:24,525 --> 00:32:26,069
than those who govern it.

615
00:32:31,491 --> 00:32:32,700
How are you going to prove

616
00:32:32,784 --> 00:32:34,369
that you did not kill Nimfa Naig?

617
00:32:34,744 --> 00:32:36,829
-Do you have proof?
-Thank you very much.

618
00:32:36,913 --> 00:32:38,623
[Georgina] That's enough
questions for today.

619
00:32:38,706 --> 00:32:39,499
Thank you.

620
00:32:39,582 --> 00:32:41,584
[overlapping dialogue]

621
00:32:47,632 --> 00:32:49,509
[Diego] <i>I am not going to</i>
<i>reshape Ardiente.</i>

622
00:32:50,176 --> 00:32:51,302
<i>You are.</i>

623
00:32:51,386 --> 00:32:54,430
<i>If you really love our province,</i>
<i>you'll choose what is right.</i>

624
00:32:55,515 --> 00:32:56,933
<i>You will choose change.</i>

625
00:32:57,475 --> 00:32:59,644
<i>For a town where the people</i>
<i>hold more power…</i>

626
00:32:59,727 --> 00:33:00,937
I'm voting for the Ardientes.

627
00:33:01,020 --> 00:33:04,107
-<i>…than those who govern it.</i>
-They've governed us for years,

628
00:33:04,190 --> 00:33:05,400
and we're doing okay.

629
00:33:05,817 --> 00:33:07,610
Why do we need change?

630
00:33:07,694 --> 00:33:10,530
[woman] But our lives
aren't getting better.

631
00:33:10,905 --> 00:33:14,158
They keep getting richer,
while we keep getting poorer.

632
00:33:14,242 --> 00:33:17,870
[woman 2] While Mayor Arnaldo's
busy preparing for his wedding,

633
00:33:17,954 --> 00:33:22,417
he won't notice the dilapidated
roads and bridges.

634
00:33:22,875 --> 00:33:24,252
[man] Well, he's excited to get married.

635
00:33:24,335 --> 00:33:27,046
Infrastructure projects
can wait, but his bride can't.

636
00:33:28,548 --> 00:33:30,008
[man] What's this? <i>Adobo</i> or<i> menudo?</i>

637
00:33:30,091 --> 00:33:31,384
<i>Caldereta</i>?

638
00:33:31,759 --> 00:33:33,594
Keep eating. It's on me.

639
00:33:36,597 --> 00:33:38,349
Great job with the press today, Diego.

640
00:33:38,433 --> 00:33:39,642
Powerful statements.

641
00:33:40,101 --> 00:33:42,603
And most importantly,
everything you said was true.

642
00:33:42,687 --> 00:33:45,356
That's a trait
every leader should possess.

643
00:33:45,815 --> 00:33:46,941
Thank you, Aunt Camia.

644
00:33:47,358 --> 00:33:49,986
And they need to be handsome too!

645
00:33:50,069 --> 00:33:51,070
Nanny!

646
00:33:51,404 --> 00:33:52,321
Dignified…

647
00:33:52,405 --> 00:33:54,407
-Uncle!
-and kind-hearted.

648
00:33:55,241 --> 00:33:57,452
Hey, hey, hey. What's that?

649
00:33:58,119 --> 00:34:00,329
What did they do to you?

650
00:34:00,413 --> 00:34:01,414
It's nothing, Nanny.

651
00:34:02,081 --> 00:34:03,291
What do you mean it's nothing?

652
00:34:03,374 --> 00:34:06,461
Who did that to you? Tell me!

653
00:34:06,794 --> 00:34:08,129
They're in the hospital.

654
00:34:08,463 --> 00:34:09,464
They're recuperating.

655
00:34:10,715 --> 00:34:11,966
You gave them a good beating?

656
00:34:13,801 --> 00:34:15,136
Serves them right.

657
00:34:15,219 --> 00:34:19,015
-Uncle, Nanny, have a seat.
-We brought you some food.

658
00:34:19,098 --> 00:34:20,892
And your favorite, fritters.

659
00:34:20,975 --> 00:34:22,310
Wow.

660
00:34:22,810 --> 00:34:24,062
Good day.

661
00:34:24,520 --> 00:34:28,149
[Loring] Here, we also brought…

662
00:34:28,733 --> 00:34:30,151
your other favorites.

663
00:34:30,234 --> 00:34:31,986
-Thank you, Nanny.
-Here.

664
00:34:32,070 --> 00:34:34,906
[soft piano music playing]

665
00:34:37,575 --> 00:34:38,576
Mister Fernan.

666
00:34:43,790 --> 00:34:44,832
Diego.

667
00:34:46,793 --> 00:34:49,670
Tell me what really happened to Nimfa.

668
00:34:51,422 --> 00:34:53,299
Who killed her?

669
00:35:05,895 --> 00:35:07,605
Wait for my signal.

670
00:35:07,688 --> 00:35:09,941
[suspenseful music playing]

671
00:35:12,777 --> 00:35:13,778
[Arnaldo clears throat]

672
00:35:14,987 --> 00:35:15,988
Hon.

673
00:35:16,447 --> 00:35:17,448
Does it still hurt?

674
00:35:17,865 --> 00:35:19,325
No. It was nothing.

675
00:35:20,284 --> 00:35:21,369
I feel better.

676
00:35:21,452 --> 00:35:23,496
Uh… All the pain went away
when you vouched for me

677
00:35:23,579 --> 00:35:24,872
in front of the press.

678
00:35:25,998 --> 00:35:27,667
You know, we really make a good team.

679
00:35:28,126 --> 00:35:30,545
Of course, hon. Just like what you said,

680
00:35:30,628 --> 00:35:32,839
I am the future first lady
of this province,

681
00:35:32,922 --> 00:35:36,968
that's why I need to meet your
expectations and of the people.

682
00:35:38,469 --> 00:35:39,595
That's right.

683
00:35:39,679 --> 00:35:41,430
But, hon, let me remind you.

684
00:35:41,514 --> 00:35:44,600
I'm not meek like most other first ladies.

685
00:35:45,143 --> 00:35:46,185
I'll be fierce.

686
00:35:46,269 --> 00:35:49,438
I'll show everyone I can protect myself…

687
00:35:49,939 --> 00:35:51,023
from anyone.

688
00:35:51,899 --> 00:35:53,025
Just what I like.

689
00:35:53,401 --> 00:35:55,111
Actually, you know what, you need a gun.

690
00:35:57,905 --> 00:35:58,906
No, hon.

691
00:35:58,990 --> 00:35:59,949
I already have my own.

692
00:36:00,908 --> 00:36:03,161
But speaking of guns…

693
00:36:04,120 --> 00:36:06,455
Where's the rifle I gave you as a gift?

694
00:36:06,539 --> 00:36:08,749
You told me you had a gun collection.

695
00:36:09,458 --> 00:36:12,253
That's why I gave you a rifle.
But I haven't seen you use it.

696
00:36:12,336 --> 00:36:13,462
It's still with me.

697
00:36:13,880 --> 00:36:15,882
Actually, it has a special place
in my armory.

698
00:36:16,382 --> 00:36:18,968
-Armory?
-Yes. I'll show you.

699
00:36:19,051 --> 00:36:20,970
-You have your own armory?
-Of course.

700
00:36:21,762 --> 00:36:23,055
-I'll show you.
-[chuckles]

701
00:36:23,139 --> 00:36:24,140
You'll be impressed.

702
00:36:29,520 --> 00:36:30,938
The Ardientes.

703
00:36:31,022 --> 00:36:32,690
They were the ones who killed Nimfa.

704
00:36:34,317 --> 00:36:35,943
How did that happen?!

705
00:36:37,111 --> 00:36:38,029
Mister Fernan.

706
00:36:39,572 --> 00:36:40,990
Emilia used her.

707
00:36:44,702 --> 00:36:46,287
This is Nimfa's cellphone.

708
00:36:47,121 --> 00:36:50,750
You'll find their text message
exchanges there.

709
00:37:00,343 --> 00:37:02,511
The last message she sent me
is still here.

710
00:37:03,804 --> 00:37:05,014
She said…

711
00:37:07,141 --> 00:37:08,226
"Dad…

712
00:37:14,649 --> 00:37:16,317
I love you so much."

713
00:37:22,406 --> 00:37:23,407
Mister Fernan…

714
00:37:25,076 --> 00:37:26,327
don't worry.

715
00:37:26,410 --> 00:37:28,246
We'll seek justice

716
00:37:28,955 --> 00:37:30,414
for your daughter's death.

717
00:37:46,389 --> 00:37:48,766
Wow, hon! You have so many guns!

718
00:37:50,726 --> 00:37:52,770
Have you used every single one of them?

719
00:37:52,853 --> 00:37:54,313
Well, most of them.

720
00:37:55,606 --> 00:37:57,149
Hey. Check this out.

721
00:38:05,283 --> 00:38:06,284
The one from you.

722
00:38:10,037 --> 00:38:11,789
Thanks, hon.
You're taking good care of it.

723
00:38:11,872 --> 00:38:12,790
Of course.

724
00:38:15,167 --> 00:38:17,336
That one. I like that one, hon.

725
00:38:17,420 --> 00:38:19,171
It's small and handy.

726
00:38:20,047 --> 00:38:21,674
Oh, okay. Wait.

727
00:38:24,552 --> 00:38:26,095
Colt Defender.

728
00:38:27,638 --> 00:38:29,056
It's explosive…

729
00:38:29,140 --> 00:38:30,474
and has intense firepower.

730
00:38:31,642 --> 00:38:32,935
Very powerful,

731
00:38:33,019 --> 00:38:34,270
just like me.

732
00:38:34,895 --> 00:38:37,064
-Yes, just like you.
-[Arnaldo chuckles]

733
00:38:38,316 --> 00:38:39,483
Hon,

734
00:38:39,567 --> 00:38:40,443
can I have this?

735
00:38:41,319 --> 00:38:42,320
Sure.

736
00:38:42,820 --> 00:38:44,071
Thank you!

737
00:38:44,155 --> 00:38:47,408
But wait, I'll need a license to use this,

738
00:38:47,491 --> 00:38:49,910
just in case the need arises.

739
00:38:51,495 --> 00:38:55,416
Okay, all the licenses are compiled here.

740
00:38:55,499 --> 00:38:56,792
You don't have to worry.

741
00:38:58,252 --> 00:38:59,337
That's amazing, hon.

742
00:38:59,420 --> 00:39:02,631
All these are under your name? Really?

743
00:39:02,715 --> 00:39:04,133
[tense music playing]

744
00:39:04,216 --> 00:39:05,468
[chuckles]

745
00:39:08,095 --> 00:39:09,513
-[phone ringing]
-Wait.

746
00:39:11,015 --> 00:39:11,849
[phone ringing]

747
00:39:11,932 --> 00:39:13,100
It must be work.

748
00:39:14,060 --> 00:39:15,353
Oh, it's Grandpa. Excuse me.

749
00:39:19,857 --> 00:39:20,941
Hello, Grandpa?

750
00:39:21,859 --> 00:39:22,943
Hello, Arnaldo?

751
00:39:23,027 --> 00:39:25,071
Grandpa, I can't hear you. Hello?

752
00:39:25,154 --> 00:39:27,114
Yeah, we need to talk. Uh…

753
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:28,949
Come to my office.

754
00:39:30,785 --> 00:39:32,578
Uh, okay, Grandpa.

755
00:39:34,038 --> 00:39:35,164
[scoffs]

756
00:39:35,247 --> 00:39:36,248
Choppy.

757
00:39:41,462 --> 00:39:43,547
Ivy, I have to go to Grandpa's office.

758
00:39:43,631 --> 00:39:44,423
He needs me.

759
00:39:44,507 --> 00:39:45,633
-Okay, hon.
-I need to go.

760
00:39:45,716 --> 00:39:47,009
-Can I stay here?
-Sure.

761
00:39:47,718 --> 00:39:48,719
-I'll be back.
-Okay.

762
00:39:48,803 --> 00:39:53,224
[suspenseful music playing]

763
00:40:10,783 --> 00:40:14,370
[suspenseful music continues]

764
00:40:28,426 --> 00:40:31,137
I spoke to the judge
who's handling your case.

765
00:40:31,595 --> 00:40:33,431
And she won't inhibit the case.

766
00:40:33,848 --> 00:40:36,225
She's obviously afraid of the Ardientes.

767
00:40:36,892 --> 00:40:39,311
I offered protection, but she insisted.

768
00:40:39,770 --> 00:40:41,897
Do you want me to talk to her, Attorney?

769
00:40:42,648 --> 00:40:43,774
I know how it feels

770
00:40:43,858 --> 00:40:46,068
to have your life
controlled by the Ardientes.

771
00:40:47,069 --> 00:40:50,030
Maybe I could convince her
to not be afraid and fight.

772
00:40:51,073 --> 00:40:52,324
That's a very good idea.

773
00:40:52,741 --> 00:40:53,742
I'll go with you.

774
00:40:54,702 --> 00:40:57,163
[Camia] Diego, I'm sorry
we won't be staying long.

775
00:40:57,746 --> 00:40:59,290
Aunt Camia, be careful.

776
00:40:59,373 --> 00:41:01,959
The Ardientes might be
watching that judge.

777
00:41:02,460 --> 00:41:03,502
-Thank you.
-All right.

778
00:41:13,971 --> 00:41:15,055
You know,

779
00:41:15,139 --> 00:41:19,518
we have to get this survey
while this issue is still hot.

780
00:41:20,394 --> 00:41:22,104
Okay. I'll take care of it, Grandpa.

781
00:41:22,188 --> 00:41:26,233
[Julio] Yes, this will work in our favor.

782
00:41:26,317 --> 00:41:27,359
Hon?

783
00:41:27,735 --> 00:41:28,944
-Hon?
-Sorry, I overheard you.

784
00:41:29,028 --> 00:41:30,446
Maybe I can help?

785
00:41:31,238 --> 00:41:32,781
Hey, Ivy.

786
00:41:33,282 --> 00:41:34,325
I mean…

787
00:41:34,408 --> 00:41:36,535
your offer is welcome, but…

788
00:41:37,244 --> 00:41:39,747
Arnaldo can handle it by himself.

789
00:41:40,289 --> 00:41:41,332
Besides,

790
00:41:41,916 --> 00:41:44,293
the last time you tried to help us,

791
00:41:44,627 --> 00:41:45,794
it didn't…

792
00:41:45,878 --> 00:41:47,755
turn out too well for us.

793
00:41:48,631 --> 00:41:49,798
Congressman.

794
00:41:49,882 --> 00:41:53,052
It seems like your
grandpa is saying I'm bad luck.

795
00:41:53,135 --> 00:41:57,014
Hey. No! No! No! Don't get me wrong, Ivy.

796
00:41:57,097 --> 00:41:58,557
You're not bad luck!

797
00:41:59,099 --> 00:42:00,184
It's just…

798
00:42:00,809 --> 00:42:02,186
W-what's this?

799
00:42:03,062 --> 00:42:05,356
-What?
-Arnaldo can handle it!

800
00:42:05,856 --> 00:42:08,108
My grandson doesn't need help.

801
00:42:08,609 --> 00:42:10,861
And you have a lot of things to attend to.

802
00:42:10,945 --> 00:42:12,279
More important things!

803
00:42:12,696 --> 00:42:13,697
Like…

804
00:42:15,574 --> 00:42:18,953
your engagement party with Arnaldo!

805
00:42:19,036 --> 00:42:19,954
That's a big thing!

806
00:42:20,037 --> 00:42:21,413
-That's right.
-We need to invite…

807
00:42:21,497 --> 00:42:23,249
all the important people.

808
00:42:23,582 --> 00:42:25,167
So you should attend to that. I mean…

809
00:42:25,668 --> 00:42:28,420
Let the men handle the politics,

810
00:42:28,504 --> 00:42:30,256
and let the women…

811
00:42:31,590 --> 00:42:34,718
tend to the… to the kitchen!

812
00:42:35,302 --> 00:42:36,804
Get it? There.

813
00:42:37,805 --> 00:42:38,889
Division of labor.

814
00:42:41,809 --> 00:42:42,893
Something like that.

815
00:42:43,519 --> 00:42:44,520
Hmm.

816
00:42:47,648 --> 00:42:49,441
You're early today, Judge De Jesus.

817
00:42:50,234 --> 00:42:52,570
Yes. I'll wait for my driver here.

818
00:42:52,653 --> 00:42:53,571
Sure, ma'am.

819
00:42:53,654 --> 00:42:54,613
[man] Sir, where's…

820
00:42:54,697 --> 00:42:55,948
-Yes, sir?
-Attorney Mallari?

821
00:42:56,031 --> 00:42:57,700
He's inside. I'll take you there.

822
00:43:01,870 --> 00:43:03,872
[tense music playing]

823
00:43:06,667 --> 00:43:09,545
Judge De Jesus, please come with us.

824
00:43:09,628 --> 00:43:11,046
Who are you? What do you want?

825
00:43:12,965 --> 00:43:14,174
Judge.

826
00:43:14,258 --> 00:43:16,176
You don't want to make a scene, do you?

827
00:43:17,928 --> 00:43:19,221
Please come with us.

828
00:43:19,638 --> 00:43:22,182
[suspenseful music playing]

829
00:43:34,236 --> 00:43:35,237
[man] Get in.

830
00:43:37,114 --> 00:43:38,073
Get in.

831
00:44:07,144 --> 00:44:10,397
We arrived just in time
to meet with Judge De Jesus.

832
00:44:11,231 --> 00:44:13,901
-What can I do for you, ma'am?
-We're here for Judge De Jesus.

833
00:44:13,984 --> 00:44:16,695
Is she inside? I wanted to talk to her.

834
00:44:16,779 --> 00:44:19,031
She just left.

835
00:44:19,114 --> 00:44:20,616
Too bad, you just missed her.

836
00:44:21,367 --> 00:44:25,204
Sir, has Judge De Jesus already left?

837
00:44:25,579 --> 00:44:26,872
Yes, sir.

838
00:44:26,955 --> 00:44:28,332
Haven't you seen her?

839
00:44:28,415 --> 00:44:29,416
No.

840
00:44:30,250 --> 00:44:31,418
Where did she go?

841
00:44:32,544 --> 00:44:35,714
[ominous music playing]

842
00:44:51,855 --> 00:44:52,856
Hello.

843
00:44:53,816 --> 00:44:55,234
So…

844
00:44:56,610 --> 00:44:58,862
Who did Emilia ask you to find?

845
00:45:04,827 --> 00:45:06,370
Miss Lily Cruz.

846
00:45:08,747 --> 00:45:09,998
Lily Cruz?

847
00:45:11,500 --> 00:45:14,253
Has she been looking for Lily
for a while now?

848
00:45:14,336 --> 00:45:16,505
No. She ordered me just recently.

849
00:45:16,588 --> 00:45:19,091
But I think it's important
for her to find Lily.

850
00:45:20,592 --> 00:45:21,718
Really?

851
00:45:24,888 --> 00:45:26,265
Lily Cruz, huh?

852
00:45:43,782 --> 00:45:44,992
Don't be afraid.

853
00:45:45,617 --> 00:45:46,827
I won't hurt you.

854
00:45:47,369 --> 00:45:49,830
In fact, I have something for you.

855
00:45:50,998 --> 00:45:52,082
Rufo!

856
00:46:02,134 --> 00:46:03,552
What is this for?

857
00:46:05,304 --> 00:46:07,347
Judge De Jesus, I know you're smart.

858
00:46:07,431 --> 00:46:09,725
So, you should know what that's for.

859
00:46:12,060 --> 00:46:14,605
Who do you want to get acquitted?

860
00:46:15,189 --> 00:46:16,773
I like you, Judge Rotico.

861
00:46:17,524 --> 00:46:18,775
You're quick to catch on.

862
00:46:20,110 --> 00:46:22,112
[sighs] Judge De Jesus,

863
00:46:23,155 --> 00:46:26,283
I want you to dismiss
the case against Diego Torillo.

864
00:46:27,576 --> 00:46:30,078
And you have to replace her, Judge Rotico.

865
00:46:31,038 --> 00:46:32,164
Also…

866
00:46:32,706 --> 00:46:34,249
I want you to move the hearing…

867
00:46:34,917 --> 00:46:37,169
of Diego's case to another province.

868
00:46:39,129 --> 00:46:41,006
Are you against the Ardientes?

869
00:46:42,132 --> 00:46:43,300
Let's say I am.

870
00:46:45,427 --> 00:46:49,223
And now that I have power over the law…

871
00:46:51,308 --> 00:46:53,143
I will make the Ardientes suffer.

872
00:47:01,026 --> 00:47:02,736
[Ivy] I'm sure the Ardientes

873
00:47:02,819 --> 00:47:04,488
are behind Judge De Jesus' disappearance!

874
00:47:04,571 --> 00:47:05,906
They're going to delay the hearing

875
00:47:05,989 --> 00:47:08,075
to make sure the survey
is released beforehand.

876
00:47:08,158 --> 00:47:10,661
Well, let's just hope
that Diego will win the survey.

877
00:47:10,744 --> 00:47:12,579
That way, we have leverage
to pressure the court

878
00:47:12,663 --> 00:47:14,289
to replace Judge De Jesus.

879
00:47:14,373 --> 00:47:16,458
I'm certain Diego's going to win.

880
00:47:25,259 --> 00:47:26,510
Sir, please answer this survey.

881
00:47:27,177 --> 00:47:28,262
Here you go, sir.

882
00:47:28,345 --> 00:47:30,430
[tense music playing]

883
00:47:30,514 --> 00:47:33,934
[no audible dialogue]

884
00:47:34,017 --> 00:47:37,020
[Pandoy] Diego Torillo for
the new Ardiente!

885
00:47:37,104 --> 00:47:38,605
-Vote for Diego!
-Here you go!

886
00:47:38,689 --> 00:47:39,481
Please vote for him!

887
00:47:39,565 --> 00:47:41,358
Vote for Diego! Vote for Diego!

888
00:47:42,025 --> 00:47:43,652
That's Diego Torillo, don't forget!

889
00:47:43,735 --> 00:47:44,903
-Good day!
-He's the governor…

890
00:47:44,987 --> 00:47:46,780
-of the people!
-Please vote for Diego.

891
00:47:46,863 --> 00:47:50,576
[tense music playing]

892
00:48:00,043 --> 00:48:02,379
WHO ARE YOU GOING TO VOTE
FOR IN THE UPCOMING ELECTION?

893
00:48:04,131 --> 00:48:05,299
[no audible dialogue]

894
00:48:07,342 --> 00:48:11,471
-Diego! Diego!
-Diego for the new Ardiente!

895
00:48:11,555 --> 00:48:13,473
-Diego for the new Ardiente!
-Let's vote for Diego Torillo!

896
00:48:13,557 --> 00:48:14,641
-Diego for the new Ardiente!
-Diego!

897
00:48:14,725 --> 00:48:16,560
Diego! Diego!

898
00:48:16,643 --> 00:48:19,980
-Diego! Diego!
-Diego for the new Ardiente!

899
00:48:20,063 --> 00:48:23,525
[suspenseful music playing]

900
00:48:30,198 --> 00:48:31,283
Thanks.

901
00:48:32,367 --> 00:48:33,910
Thank you. Thanks.

902
00:48:35,579 --> 00:48:36,580
Thank you.

903
00:48:38,081 --> 00:48:40,751
[suspenseful music continues playing]

904
00:48:44,254 --> 00:48:46,006
-[shouts] Grandpa! Mom!
-What?

905
00:48:46,840 --> 00:48:48,008
Hon!

906
00:48:48,091 --> 00:48:49,051
This isn't true!

907
00:48:49,134 --> 00:48:51,970
Impossible! That's impossible!

908
00:48:52,054 --> 00:48:54,306
That is not true! Diego beat me?!

909
00:48:54,389 --> 00:48:57,392
I don't believe it! I don't believe it!

910
00:48:58,977 --> 00:49:00,187
[tense music playing]

911
00:49:06,068 --> 00:49:07,152
[Ivy] Arnaldo…

912
00:49:08,236 --> 00:49:09,988
[Julio] How did this dog…

913
00:49:11,406 --> 00:49:12,449
beat you?!

914
00:49:12,991 --> 00:49:13,825
Well?!

915
00:49:15,160 --> 00:49:16,662
[thuds]

916
00:49:16,745 --> 00:49:18,705
[tense music playing]

917
00:49:24,086 --> 00:49:28,715
<i>We Ardientes are the rightful</i>
<i>leaders of this town.</i>

918
00:49:28,799 --> 00:49:32,511
<i>That is why we're going</i>
<i>to have Diego killed.</i>

919
00:49:33,303 --> 00:49:34,721
[detainee] <i>Congressman's orders.</i>

920
00:49:34,805 --> 00:49:36,473
[Diego grunts and groans]

921
00:49:37,099 --> 00:49:39,267
<i>Why don't you accompany me?</i>

922
00:49:39,351 --> 00:49:40,644
[Ivy] <i>I'm sorry. I'm not interested.</i>

923
00:49:40,727 --> 00:49:42,688
<i>Even if it's about Lily Cruz?</i>

924
00:49:43,855 --> 00:49:45,232
[Ivy] <i>I have a bad feeling about this.</i>

925
00:49:45,315 --> 00:49:46,149
<i>Let's go home.</i>

926
00:49:47,567 --> 00:49:49,569
[Natalie laughing]

927
00:49:49,653 --> 00:49:51,196
<i>What's your problem, Natalie?</i>

928
00:49:51,279 --> 00:49:53,240
[Natalie] <i>My poor father trusted you!</i>

929
00:49:53,740 --> 00:49:55,951
<i>It's payback time, Emilia!</i>

930
00:49:56,827 --> 00:50:00,038
[theme music playing]
